From fbed211c6f4352335a653a5d384e3e655cf7633e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: M0n7y5 <17201053+M0n7y5@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:54:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winepipewire.drv: Report a discarded malformed capture
 buffer.

A dequeued buffer that fails metadata validation is counted and requeued, so
its audio is dropped.  Nothing recorded the loss: no sequence is consumed and
the flag was left clear, so the next packet reached the application looking
contiguous.  That was the last path in the capture chain that could lose audio
without saying so.

Charge it to the next slot published, like the clamp and the all-slots-held
drop.  Capture only; the same validation guards the render path, where a
missed cycle is an underrun rather than lost input.

This is inspection-only.  Reaching it needs the server to hand over a buffer
with no datas, a null data pointer or a null chunk, which no probe here can
provoke without patching PipeWire, and bad_buffer_count has stayed at zero in
every run.
---
 dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c b/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
index d07e1d13034..3ecab8fd397 100644
--- a/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
+++ b/dlls/winepipewire.drv/pipewire.c
@@ -1811,6 +1811,14 @@ static void on_stream_process(void *data)
         !(d = &buf->datas[0])->data || !d->chunk)
     {
         __atomic_add_fetch(&stream->bad_buffer_count, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED);
+        if (stream->dataflow == eCapture)
+        {
+            /* The buffer is discarded, so audio was lost.  Charge it to the
+             * next slot published, the same as a clamp or an all-slots-held
+             * drop; without this the application sees the gap with nothing to
+             * explain it.  Producer-private, so a plain store is right. */
+            stream->cap_lost = TRUE;
+        }
         pw_stream_queue_buffer(stream->pw, b);
         return;
     }
-- 
